## Highlights
Fe(II)MOFs are synthesized via hydrothermal self-assembled coordination.   
Fe(II)MOFs exhibit diverse active sites and electron-donating properties.   
$\mathsf{a F e(I I)}$ acts as an effective electron donor for both persulfate and dioxygen.   
Direct electron transfer to SMX molecule by the attack of $\mathrm{SO}_{4}$ ·- was proposed.
